Package: homelab-keepalived
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36), libyaml-libyaml-perl, keepalived, nftables
Recommends: homelab-agent
Description: VRRP virtual-IP failover (keepalived) for the homelab-* edge
 Floats a public virtual IP (VIP) between two or more internet-facing
 fleet nodes using keepalived/VRRP, so if the node that currently owns the
 public IP dies, a standby node claims it -- sending a gratuitous ARP so
 the upstream AT&T gateway follows the IP to the new node's MAC with no
 gateway reconfiguration (the gateway routes the public subnet to the LAN
 and resolves each public IP by ARP, so this "just works" with no AT&T
 side change).
 .
 Reads an editable /etc/homelab/keepalived/vrrp.yml (priority, VRRP
 interface + unicast peers on the internal plane, the VIP and its public
 interface, the master-only default route) and regenerates
 /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf plus a safe (no-flush) VRRP firewall
 drop-in. VRRP advertisements run as unicast on the internal service
 plane; the VIP and the master-only default route move together on
 failover. Pairs with homelab-webproxy / homelab-haproxy /
 homelab-dnsdist, which bind 0.0.0.0 and so serve the VIP automatically
 whenever this node holds it.
